# Commits that moved or reformatted code without changing behaviour.
#
# `git blame` follows the last commit to touch a line, so a formatting sweep or
# a file split re-points every line in it at that sweep. The tests in this repo
# encode specific past failures -- a bind precheck, a watchdog liveness window, a
# regulatory reconciler -- and knowing which change introduced a line is how the
# reasoning behind it is recovered. Losing that to a whitespace commit is a real
# cost, so those commits are listed here instead.
#
# Enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a commit that provably changed no behaviour. If in doubt, leave it
# out: a wrongly-listed commit hides the change that actually caused a bug.

